WEBVTT

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.731
Kira, we've got
six Byzatium transports

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.896
coming in this afternoon.

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:06.098
I've got to have
more cargo space.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:08.802
All right, have them off-load

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:10.571
into Cargo Bays 3 and 4,
but that's it.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.601
We are pushing
our storage capacity as it is.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:13.737
Well, that reminds me...

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.441
we got a message last night
saying the Byzallians

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:17.313
want to move their
conference up by a week.

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:23.186
I haven't had a chance to read
through last night's reports.

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:25.248
Is there anything else
I should know?

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.451
Well, um...

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:28.859
What?

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.354
Starfleet wants
a complete report done

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:34.458
on our computer
calibration subroutine.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:37.265
The whole subroutine?

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:38.292
When?

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:39.999
Tomorrow.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:51.009
Major, the scheduled transport's
been delayed

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:53.517
and I need those medical
supplies by the end of the week.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.850
We can't spare a runabout

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:56.856
to go all the way
to Vulcan right now.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.755
I'm supposed to be setting up
a field hospital

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.453
for a new colony
on Campor III next week.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.154
And if I don't get
those medical supplies

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.685
then the entire
colonization schedule

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:04.958
could be set back
by at least...

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.464
Listen to me!

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.763
You can't have a runabout.

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:10.565
You cannot get
your medical supplies

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:13.436
and I don't give a damn about
the colonization schedule!

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:14.872
Those colonists can make do

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.808
with a box of bandages
for all I care.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:17.969
Stop right there!

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:19.102
Major.

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.720
When was your last day off?

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:29.722
I don't know.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.951
What does that have to do
with anything?

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:35.017
If you can't remember,
then it's been too long.

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.557
You're off duty,
as of this moment.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:41.761
What do you mean I'm off duty?

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.735
You can't do that.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.670
Oh, yes, I can,
and not even Commander Sisko

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:48.173
can overrule my judgment
as Chief Medical Officer.

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:53.477
Now... now, wait a minute,
Julian.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:55.242
Just because I snapped...

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:59.240
My diagnosis is
that you are overworked

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:01.845
and suffering
from extreme stress

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.947
and borderline exhaustion.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:06.583
As for my prescription...

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:09.522
Follow me.

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:21.797
Karvino juice

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:24.071
Lorvan crackers

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.135
a holosuite program

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:28.977
a jumja stick
and gambling tokens.

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.676
Now, at least two of these items

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:33.811
must be used and fully enjoyed
before you leave this facility.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:34.979
Julian, I...

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.648
I'll be giving you a full report
of her activities, Doctor.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.453
And if I hear you
didn't completely relax

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.652
and enjoy yourself tonight

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.854
we'll do this every night
until you do.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.961
Have fun!

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:02.343
Looks like you've got
your evening all planned.

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:05.010
Hope you've got room
for the unexpected.

00:05:06.404 --> 00:05:07.769
Welcome aboard, Commander.

00:05:07.805 --> 00:05:09.636
Thank you.

00:05:09.674 --> 00:05:11.301
Call me Will.

00:05:11.342 --> 00:05:13.810
What brings you to Deep Space 9?

00:05:13.845 --> 00:05:15.210
Strictly pleasure.

00:05:15.246 --> 00:05:17.578
Actually, I have built up
about three months of leave

00:05:17.615 --> 00:05:19.105
and Dr. Crusher finally insisted

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:20.378
that I take some of it.

00:05:20.418 --> 00:05:21.942
She nearly shoved me
out of the airlock.

00:05:23.187 --> 00:05:25.678
Well, DS9 isn't exactly
known as a vacation spot.

00:05:25.723 --> 00:05:28.556
Actually, I was just passing
through on my way to Risa.

00:05:28.593 --> 00:05:29.753
The last time I was here

00:05:29.794 --> 00:05:32.422
I was only able to spend
a couple of hours at Quark's.

00:05:32.463 --> 00:05:34.863
But, by the time I left,
I had all of his latinum

00:05:34.899 --> 00:05:36.662
and a date
with one of his dabo girls

00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:38.601
so I thought
I might try my luck again.

00:05:38.636 --> 00:05:40.365
You be careful.

00:05:40.405 --> 00:05:42.703
Quark's dabo wheel's been
a little stingy lately

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:45.641
and one of his dabo girls
is dating my son.

00:05:45.677 --> 00:05:49.204
In that case, I think I'd better
spend my time in the holosuite.

00:05:49.247 --> 00:05:51.306
It sounds safer,
all the way around.

00:05:58.356 --> 00:05:59.380
Who's in there?

00:06:00.425 --> 00:06:01.483
What?

00:06:01.526 --> 00:06:03.050
Who's in with Benjamin?

00:06:03.094 --> 00:06:07.360
Oh, it's Will... Commander
Will Riker from the Enterprise.

00:06:07.398 --> 00:06:10.265
Will Riker?

00:06:10.301 --> 00:06:12.633
You know him?

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:13.694
Yeah.

00:06:13.738 --> 00:06:15.933
I met him a year ago at Quark's.

00:06:16.007 --> 00:06:17.599
He's, uh, quite a dabo player.

00:06:17.642 --> 00:06:18.939
Hmm.

00:06:18.977 --> 00:06:20.911
Do you know him?

00:06:20.945 --> 00:06:22.503
Yes, a little.

00:06:22.547 --> 00:06:26.449
I met him at Quark's last night.

00:06:26.484 --> 00:06:29.146
You met him last night, and...?

00:06:29.187 --> 00:06:30.586
And we talked.

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:33.589
And then?

00:06:33.625 --> 00:06:36.651
And then we talked.

00:06:36.694 --> 00:06:39.288
For three hours.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:41.662
No, we just talked.

00:06:41.699 --> 00:06:44.862
And, yes, he's a warm,
charming man...

00:06:44.902 --> 00:06:47.427
but I'm involved with someone.

00:06:47.472 --> 00:06:49.838
Of course.

00:06:53.011 --> 00:06:56.412
So why do you keep glancing
back at Sisko's office?

00:06:56.447 --> 00:06:57.937
If you can find the time

00:06:57.982 --> 00:07:00.314
you have an open invitation
for dinner with me and Jake.

00:07:00.351 --> 00:07:02.251
Thank you.
I may take you up on that.

00:07:02.286 --> 00:07:04.277
I hope you're not here
for another loan.

00:07:04.322 --> 00:07:05.789
Don't tell me you've forgotten

00:07:05.823 --> 00:07:07.723
who staked you
three strips of latinum

00:07:07.759 --> 00:07:09.420
when your winning streak
ran dry.

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:11.257
I'm sorry.
Of course.

00:07:11.295 --> 00:07:12.592
Most of that night's
still a blur.

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:13.824
How have you been, Dax?

00:07:13.865 --> 00:07:14.832
Fine.

00:07:14.866 --> 00:07:16.094
Well, I'd better
get out of your way.

00:07:16.134 --> 00:07:17.567
I know you all have work to do.

00:07:17.602 --> 00:07:19.092
Hope to see you again.

00:07:19.137 --> 00:07:20.126
Major.

00:07:20.171 --> 00:07:21.763
Commander.

00:07:41.192 --> 00:07:42.386
- Oh!
- Oh!

00:07:42.427 --> 00:07:43.485
I'm sorry.

00:07:43.528 --> 00:07:44.825
That's all right.

00:07:44.862 --> 00:07:46.159
My mind was a million
light-years away.

00:07:46.197 --> 00:07:48.165
I should have been paying
attention to where I was going.

00:07:48.199 --> 00:07:49.689
You doing some shopping?

00:07:49.734 --> 00:07:51.634
Well, actually, I was just
exploring the Promenade.

00:07:51.669 --> 00:07:53.637
I'd thought
about going into Quark's

00:07:53.671 --> 00:07:55.639
but I wasn't really in the mood.

00:07:55.673 --> 00:07:56.640
Where are you off to?

00:07:56.674 --> 00:07:57.641
I'm just getting off duty.

00:07:57.675 --> 00:07:58.801
I was about to call it a night.

00:07:58.843 --> 00:08:00.777
Oh, I see.

00:08:00.812 --> 00:08:02.746
Well, good night.

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:05.442
Good night.

00:08:07.819 --> 00:08:08.808
Commander?

00:08:10.288 --> 00:08:12.381
Would you like a tour
of the station?

00:08:13.891 --> 00:08:15.552
I'd love one.

00:08:15.593 --> 00:08:17.117
Where should we begin?

00:08:17.161 --> 00:08:19.356
We can walk along the Promenade
for a start.

00:08:19.397 --> 00:08:21.024
There's quite a bit to see here.

00:08:21.065 --> 00:08:22.089
You think we might get a chance

00:08:22.133 --> 00:08:23.430
to look at that new starship
of yours?

00:08:23.468 --> 00:08:24.435
What do you call it, the...

00:08:24.469 --> 00:08:25.561
Oh, the Defiant.

00:08:25.603 --> 00:08:26.570
Yes, the Defiant.

00:08:26.604 --> 00:08:28.333
I understand
it's quite a vessel.

00:08:28.372 --> 00:08:29.999
I'm sure that can be arranged.

00:08:41.385 --> 00:08:44.946
Please identify
for access to USS Defiant.

00:08:45.056 --> 00:08:47.684
Major Kira Nerys,
Bajoran militia.

00:08:47.725 --> 00:08:49.249
Identity confirmed.

00:08:51.062 --> 00:08:53.292
Commander William Riker,
Starfleet.

00:08:53.331 --> 00:08:55.196
Identity confirmed.

00:09:08.846 --> 00:09:12.373
Chief, I didn't know anyone else
was on board tonight.

00:09:12.416 --> 00:09:13.405
Oh, I hadn't planned to.

00:09:13.451 --> 00:09:15.078
Ouch!

00:09:15.119 --> 00:09:17.417
I was just getting
a little extra work done

00:09:17.455 --> 00:09:19.923
on the deflector
targeting arrays.

00:09:19.957 --> 00:09:23.916
Commander...
I'd heard you were aboard

00:09:23.995 --> 00:09:25.121
but I-I hadn't...

00:09:25.163 --> 00:09:26.926
There's nothing to say
to you, O'Brien.

00:09:27.031 --> 00:09:28.055
I think you know why.

00:09:30.334 --> 00:09:33.428
Well, maybe we should
come back another time.

00:09:33.471 --> 00:09:35.666
No, no, no, Major,
it's all right.

00:09:35.706 --> 00:09:37.765
I was just leaving.

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:41.103
Commander.

00:09:44.382 --> 00:09:46.475
What was all that about?

00:09:46.517 --> 00:09:47.609
Ah, it's a long story.

00:09:47.652 --> 00:09:49.279
I'd rather not get into it.

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:51.845
Let's take a look
at this ship of yours.

00:09:51.889 --> 00:09:54.949
Okay. I'll, uh, show you
the tactical systems first.

00:09:54.992 --> 00:09:56.619
Think you're going
to be surprised

00:09:56.661 --> 00:09:58.652
at how big a punch
this little ship has.

00:10:07.138 --> 00:10:08.230
Running the plasma conduit

00:10:08.272 --> 00:10:09.762
through your primary
phaser coupling

00:10:09.807 --> 00:10:11.365
has almost doubled
your phaser power.

00:10:11.409 --> 00:10:13.502
Doesn't that cut into
your warp drive efficiency?

00:10:13.544 --> 00:10:17.981
Not at all, in fact,
it's 30% %% more efficient.

00:10:18.015 --> 00:10:19.414
That's ingenious.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:20.974
I'd like to see
how it's all routed

00:10:21.085 --> 00:10:22.950
through the tactical display.

00:10:24.355 --> 00:10:27.586
Command authorization required.

00:10:27.625 --> 00:10:29.684
New security procedure.

00:10:29.727 --> 00:10:32.560
Computer,
release Bridge lockout.

00:10:32.597 --> 00:10:36.533
Authorization:
Kira Delta-5-4-7-Alpha.

00:10:40.972 --> 00:10:41.996
Thank you.

00:10:42.106 --> 00:10:43.095
Ah!

00:11:01.259 --> 00:11:02.226
What's going on?

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:04.285
I'm not sure,
but something happened

00:11:04.328 --> 00:11:05.625
to the warp core on the Defiant.

00:11:05.663 --> 00:11:07.688
It looks like it's going
to breach in 57 seconds.

00:11:07.732 --> 00:11:08.790
Anyone on board?

00:11:08.833 --> 00:11:10.664
O'Brien was working
there this morning

00:11:10.701 --> 00:11:11.929
but I don't know if he...

00:11:11.969 --> 00:11:13.561
Incoming signal
from the Defiant.

00:11:13.604 --> 00:11:14.628
It's Commander Riker.

00:11:14.672 --> 00:11:15.969
On screen.

00:11:16.007 --> 00:11:17.975
Commander Sisko,
there's been an accident.

00:11:18.009 --> 00:11:19.601
One of the plasma conduits
has exploded.

00:11:19.644 --> 00:11:21.475
Major Kira has been injured.

00:11:21.512 --> 00:11:23.912
We are 45 seconds
from a core breach.

00:11:23.948 --> 00:11:25.745
Release the docking clamps.

00:11:25.783 --> 00:11:27.978
I will get us away
from the station.

00:11:28.019 --> 00:11:30.647
We'll beam the two of you out of
there as soon as you're clear.

00:11:30.688 --> 00:11:32.212
Docking clamps released.

00:11:32.256 --> 00:11:34.156
I'm engaging thrusters.

00:11:46.804 --> 00:11:47.862
15 seconds.

00:11:47.905 --> 00:11:49.634
Lock on and beam them away,
Chief.

00:11:49.674 --> 00:11:51.403
I can't get a lock.

00:11:51.442 --> 00:11:53.000
The Defiant's shields are up.

00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:54.168
What?

00:12:01.218 --> 00:12:03.277
She's gone into warp.
I've lost them.

00:12:08.326 --> 00:12:11.227
We're beyond their sensor range.

00:12:11.262 --> 00:12:12.957
Lay in a course
for the Badlands, warp seven.

00:12:12.997 --> 00:12:14.658
Tamal, secure that conduit.

00:12:14.699 --> 00:12:16.064
Right.

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:17.397
Course laid in.

00:12:17.435 --> 00:12:19.926
We'll be in the Badlands
in six hours.

00:12:32.016 --> 00:12:33.483
You did it, Tom.

00:12:33.517 --> 00:12:35.678
It's not over yet.

00:12:45.262 --> 00:12:47.958
Nine years ago
a transporter accident

00:12:47.998 --> 00:12:49.966
created two William T. Rikers.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:52.298
One of them returned to his ship

00:12:52.336 --> 00:12:54.463
the other was marooned
on Nervala IV.

00:12:55.673 --> 00:12:58.608
The second Riker was finally
discovered two years ago.

00:12:58.642 --> 00:13:01.167
He chose to use
his middle name, Thomas

00:13:01.212 --> 00:13:03.203
to distinguish himself
from the other Riker.

00:13:03.247 --> 00:13:06.410
The two men are physically
identical in all respects

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:09.044
right down to their DNA coding.

00:13:09.086 --> 00:13:10.951
There was no way
for the security computer

00:13:10.988 --> 00:13:13.957
to know that it was
Thomas, not William

00:13:13.991 --> 00:13:15.891
who boarded the Defiant.

00:13:15.926 --> 00:13:18.952
This is
a very entertaining story

00:13:18.996 --> 00:13:21.829
but... why am I listening to it?

00:13:25.102 --> 00:13:26.933
We have reason to believe

00:13:26.971 --> 00:13:30.372
that Thomas Riker
is a member of the Maquis.

00:13:33.811 --> 00:13:34.937
What?

00:13:34.979 --> 00:13:38.779
Thomas Riker was serving
aboard the Starship Gandhi.

00:13:38.816 --> 00:13:41.341
While he was there,
he began to express

00:13:41.385 --> 00:13:43.182
certain political opinions.

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:47.452
Opinions that supported
the Maquis and their goals.

00:13:47.491 --> 00:13:50.983
Are you telling me...

00:13:51.028 --> 00:13:57.524
that one of the most heavily
armed warships in this Quadrant

00:13:57.568 --> 00:14:01.197
is now in the hands
of Maquis terrorists?

00:14:11.515 --> 00:14:14.746
Do you have any idea
what kind of response

00:14:14.785 --> 00:14:18.118
this will provoke
from the Central Command?

00:14:18.155 --> 00:14:20.350
They'll probably want
to send ships

00:14:20.391 --> 00:14:23.417
into the Demilitarized Zone
to conduct a search.

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:24.654
We understand that

00:14:24.695 --> 00:14:27.960
but any entry into the Zone
must be a joint operation

00:14:28.032 --> 00:14:30.967
between Cardassia
and the Federation.

00:14:31.001 --> 00:14:34.732
The Central Command
will not be interested

00:14:34.772 --> 00:14:37.935
in any joint operation,
Commander.

00:14:37.975 --> 00:14:39.772
They won't believe your story

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:47.512
about transporter duplicates
and security failures.

00:14:47.551 --> 00:14:49.985
They will assume that Starfleet

00:14:50.087 --> 00:14:53.545
wanted the Maquis
to have the Defiant

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:57.219
and they will respond
accordingly.

00:14:57.261 --> 00:14:59.354
And what does that mean exactly?

00:14:59.396 --> 00:15:03.264
It means they will seize
this opportunity

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:06.326
to finally eliminate the Maquis.

00:15:06.370 --> 00:15:09.828
They will send a fleet
into that Zone.

00:15:12.309 --> 00:15:16.177
Starfleet will cooperate
in a search for the Defiant

00:15:16.213 --> 00:15:19.376
but they will not allow
the Central Command

00:15:19.416 --> 00:15:23.250
to use this as an excuse
for a full-scale invasion.

00:15:23.287 --> 00:15:25.448
Of course not.

00:15:25.489 --> 00:15:28.151
So you will send your
own fleet into the Zone

00:15:28.192 --> 00:15:30.786
to protect Federation colonies.

00:15:30.828 --> 00:15:33.956
But, at some point,
the two fleets will meet

00:15:34.064 --> 00:15:37.864
tensions will rise,
nerves will fray

00:15:37.901 --> 00:15:41.860
and someone will make
the tiniest mistake.

00:15:41.905 --> 00:15:44.465
And we'll have a war
on our hands.

00:15:44.508 --> 00:15:47.909
It is a prospect
I do not relish, Commander.

00:15:47.945 --> 00:15:49.344
Neither do we.

00:15:51.148 --> 00:15:52.945
That's why we need
to work together

00:15:52.983 --> 00:15:54.814
to prevent it from happening.

00:15:54.852 --> 00:15:56.217
Well, unless I can bring

00:15:56.253 --> 00:16:00.246
something back to Central
Command to prove your good faith

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:03.350
and your willingness
to help stop the Defiant

00:16:03.394 --> 00:16:05.055
I don't believe anything

00:16:05.095 --> 00:16:08.758
can prevent this conflict
from beginning.

00:16:08.799 --> 00:16:10.596
Then bring me with you.

00:16:10.634 --> 00:16:13.125
I can help you stop the Defiant

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:15.161
and prove our good faith.

00:16:15.205 --> 00:16:18.936
I was in charge of the shipyard
where the Defiant was built.

00:16:19.043 --> 00:16:21.603
I helped design it.

00:16:21.645 --> 00:16:25.342
I know her vulnerabilities
and her weaknesses.

00:16:25.382 --> 00:16:28.943
You'll help us destroy
one of your own ships?

00:16:29.053 --> 00:16:31.715
I want to try
and disable it first.

00:16:31.755 --> 00:16:34.553
Oh, I'm sure you do.

00:16:37.594 --> 00:16:42.964
But you are in no position
to bargain here, Commander.

00:16:43.067 --> 00:16:45.627
You want to prevent a war

00:16:45.669 --> 00:16:50.834
you come back to Cardassia
with me, and you help me

00:16:50.874 --> 00:16:54.640
destroy the Defiant.

00:17:03.353 --> 00:17:08.222
I don't care who you are
or what your name is.

00:17:08.258 --> 00:17:12.092
I am sorry about lying to you,
and I'm sorry about using you.

00:17:12.129 --> 00:17:13.562
It was an operational necessity!

00:17:13.597 --> 00:17:15.565
You were a resistance fighter.

00:17:15.599 --> 00:17:16.793
You know that certain times

00:17:16.834 --> 00:17:18.563
you do things
that you're not proud of

00:17:18.602 --> 00:17:19.933
to accomplish the mission.

00:17:20.003 --> 00:17:23.404
Well, you accomplished
your mission, so now what?

00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:25.067
Everyone's going
to be looking for you.

00:17:25.109 --> 00:17:26.406
The Cardassians and Starfleet.

00:17:26.443 --> 00:17:28.604
How far do you think you're
going to get with this ship

00:17:28.645 --> 00:17:29.839
before they find you?

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:32.348
A lot farther
than people anticipate.

00:17:32.382 --> 00:17:33.576
Kalita to Riker.

00:17:33.617 --> 00:17:34.948
We've reached
the rendezvous point.

00:17:34.985 --> 00:17:37.385
I'm on my way.

00:17:43.961 --> 00:17:46.361
The other Maquis ships
just arrived.

00:17:46.396 --> 00:17:47.761
The rest of the team's ready.

00:17:47.798 --> 00:17:49.629
Lower the shields
and beam them aboard.

00:17:52.336 --> 00:17:55.464
The Maquis ships
are heading for the border, Tom.

00:17:55.506 --> 00:17:57.838
All defense systems on line
and operational.

00:17:57.875 --> 00:17:59.035
Warp power standing by.

00:18:00.677 --> 00:18:04.135
Lay in a course for the
Cardassian border, warp eight.

00:18:04.181 --> 00:18:06.513
Course already laid in.

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:08.848
This ship was built to fight.

00:18:08.886 --> 00:18:11.753
I think it's time
she got her chance.

00:18:11.788 --> 00:18:13.312
Engage.

00:18:18.061 --> 00:18:21.326
Commander's Log,
Stardate 48467.3.

00:18:21.365 --> 00:18:23.925
Gul Dukat and I have arrived
on Cardassia Prime.

00:18:24.001 --> 00:18:26.526
I'm about to do something
which goes against 20 years

00:18:26.570 --> 00:18:28.197
of Starfleet training...

00:18:28.238 --> 00:18:31.366
help an enemy hunt down
one of our own ships.

00:18:31.408 --> 00:18:35.037
This is where I'll be conducting
the search for the Defiant.

00:18:35.078 --> 00:18:41.847
From this room, I can control
every Cardassian ship, outpost

00:18:41.885 --> 00:18:44.217
and space station
anywhere in our...

00:18:47.824 --> 00:18:52.420
Ah, Commander, allow me
to introduce Korinas

00:18:52.462 --> 00:18:55.431
our observer
from the Obsidian Order.

00:18:55.465 --> 00:18:56.762
Commander Sisko.

00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:57.960
Korinas.

00:18:58.001 --> 00:19:00.765
Welcome to Cardassia Prime,
Commander.

00:19:00.804 --> 00:19:01.896
Thank you.

00:19:01.939 --> 00:19:04.271
Excuse me.

00:19:04.308 --> 00:19:07.641
Secure that console
while the human is here.

00:19:07.678 --> 00:19:11.011
Anything else classified
level 4 or above

00:19:11.048 --> 00:19:12.879
should also be secured.

00:19:15.285 --> 00:19:17.086
I'm sure you can understand

00:19:17.219 --> 00:19:19.687
that although we all respect
Gul Dukat's decision

00:19:19.721 --> 00:19:22.918
to bring you here,
we must take some precautions.

00:19:22.991 --> 00:19:24.856
Of course.

00:19:24.893 --> 00:19:26.292
I would have done the same.

00:19:27.429 --> 00:19:28.589
But then...

00:19:28.630 --> 00:19:30.120
I would have been more discreet.

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:32.733
Since you are here

00:19:32.768 --> 00:19:36.329
to provide technical expertise
on the Defiant

00:19:36.371 --> 00:19:38.635
I suggest you begin
by briefing us

00:19:38.674 --> 00:19:41.268
on the ship's
defensive capabilities.

00:19:41.310 --> 00:19:45.144
Please, describe for us
in detail

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:47.273
the weapons systems
of the Defiant

00:19:47.316 --> 00:19:49.409
beginning with
the ship's phaser array...

00:19:49.451 --> 00:19:52.545
Before we discuss weaponry,
there's a more urgent matter

00:19:52.588 --> 00:19:54.715
that I think
you should be aware of.

00:19:54.756 --> 00:19:57.088
The Defiant is equipped
with a cloaking device.

00:19:58.427 --> 00:19:59.951
I wondered
if you were going to share

00:19:59.995 --> 00:20:01.929
that little detail with us.

00:20:01.964 --> 00:20:03.158
You knew about this?

00:20:03.198 --> 00:20:05.826
The Obsidian Order
has known for some time

00:20:05.868 --> 00:20:07.699
about the loan
of a cloaking device

00:20:07.736 --> 00:20:09.328
from the Romulans
to the Federation.

00:20:09.371 --> 00:20:12.772
And the Order chose not
to share this intelligence

00:20:12.808 --> 00:20:14.503
with the Central Command?

00:20:14.543 --> 00:20:17.842
Until now, the Order had
not considered this one cloak

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:19.905
to be a threat
against Cardassia.

00:20:21.517 --> 00:20:23.542
Under our terms of agreement
with the Romulans

00:20:23.585 --> 00:20:25.246
the cloaking device
was to be used

00:20:25.287 --> 00:20:28.154
only in the Gamma Quadrant,
and then only in exchange

00:20:28.190 --> 00:20:30.852
for all our intelligence
reports on the Dominion.

00:20:30.893 --> 00:20:33.521
Well, your Lieutenant
Riker isn't likely

00:20:33.562 --> 00:20:36.395
to respect that agreement
with the Romulans

00:20:36.431 --> 00:20:40.128
and there's no way
to locate a ship under cloak.

00:20:40.169 --> 00:20:41.864
There is one possibility.

00:20:41.904 --> 00:20:44.964
The Dominion managed
to penetrate the cloak

00:20:45.007 --> 00:20:47.771
by using some kind
of antiproton beam.

00:20:47.809 --> 00:20:50.573
Can you give us the
specifications of that beam?

00:20:50.612 --> 00:20:52.546
Not precisely,
but I can give you

00:20:52.581 --> 00:20:55.015
everything we've learned
from our sensor logs.

00:20:55.050 --> 00:20:57.450
It'll give you a chance
to find the Defiant

00:20:57.486 --> 00:20:59.215
before she attacks.

00:21:03.458 --> 00:21:05.119
We're approaching
the security perimeter, Tom.

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:07.458
All right, this is it.

00:21:07.496 --> 00:21:09.794
Red Alert.

00:21:09.831 --> 00:21:11.423
Cloak the ship.

00:21:11.466 --> 00:21:13.127
Stand by, weapons.

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:27.905
Squadron Baker has arrived
at their checkpoint.

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:29.508
Transmit the go-ahead signal.

00:21:29.551 --> 00:21:33.817
We'll be in Cardassian
sensor range in five minutes.

00:21:33.855 --> 00:21:37.586
There is a perimeter alert
in the Almatha sector.

00:21:37.626 --> 00:21:39.651
Put it on the main viewer.

00:21:46.902 --> 00:21:49.598
Who's commanding the outpost
nearest that ship?

00:21:49.638 --> 00:21:51.663
Gul Toran of the Sixth Order.

00:21:51.707 --> 00:21:53.174
And he's identified the vessel.

00:21:53.208 --> 00:21:54.175
It's the Defiant.

00:21:54.209 --> 00:21:56.473
Order all warships

00:21:56.511 --> 00:21:59.275
in that sector to converge
on the Defiant.

00:22:00.616 --> 00:22:02.277
Something's wrong.

00:22:03.452 --> 00:22:06.080
Why wouldn't they be cloaked?

00:22:06.121 --> 00:22:08.988
Can you show me the sensor
information on the Defiant?

00:22:12.894 --> 00:22:14.589
The Defiant is
attacking Outpost 61.

00:22:14.630 --> 00:22:16.564
Tell Gul Toran

00:22:16.598 --> 00:22:18.862
that he has permission
to pursue the Defiant

00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:20.390
into the Demilitarized Zone.

00:22:20.435 --> 00:22:23.336
No, don't pull your ships
off the border.

00:22:23.372 --> 00:22:25.203
Commander, you don't expect me

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:27.333
to break off pursuit
of the Defiant

00:22:27.376 --> 00:22:29.207
simply because the treaty's...

00:22:29.244 --> 00:22:31.371
That's not the Defiant.
It's a decoy.

00:22:31.413 --> 00:22:33.904
They're trying to draw your
patrol ships out of position.

00:22:33.949 --> 00:22:36.383
That ship's sending
out a fake warp signature

00:22:36.418 --> 00:22:38.181
identical to the Defiant's

00:22:38.220 --> 00:22:41.212
but the phase variance and
subspace harmonics don't match.

00:22:42.291 --> 00:22:44.384
Order Toran
to break off pursuit.

00:22:44.426 --> 00:22:46.394
Have him redeploy...

00:22:46.428 --> 00:22:48.328
Sir, another perimeter alert.

00:22:48.363 --> 00:22:49.955
Outpost 47 has detected

00:22:49.998 --> 00:22:52.159
a cloaked ship
with their antiproton beam.

00:22:53.568 --> 00:22:56.366
Tell Toran to head
for Outpost 47.

00:22:56.405 --> 00:22:58.373
The Defiant has de-cloaked

00:22:58.407 --> 00:23:00.534
and has begun
to attack the outpost.

00:23:01.943 --> 00:23:03.808
We've lost contact
with Outpost 47.

00:23:07.149 --> 00:23:08.878
Incoming message from Gul Toran.

00:23:08.917 --> 00:23:10.248
The Defiant has re-cloaked

00:23:10.285 --> 00:23:14.813
and its last known heading
was 148 mark 215.

00:23:16.892 --> 00:23:21.556
It's headed directly into the
heart of Cardassian territory.

00:23:23.298 --> 00:23:26.392
Commander Sisko,
you should be commended.

00:23:26.435 --> 00:23:29.700
I only wish we had someone with
such keen tactical instincts

00:23:29.738 --> 00:23:34.505
who could have prevented
this invasion of our territory.

00:23:44.486 --> 00:23:46.317
We're past
the security perimeter

00:23:46.355 --> 00:23:47.982
out of their sensor range.

00:23:48.023 --> 00:23:50.992
They're using antiproton beams
to scan for us.

00:23:51.026 --> 00:23:52.653
Adjust the cloak's
resonance frequency

00:23:52.694 --> 00:23:53.854
so they can't detect us again.

00:23:53.895 --> 00:23:55.089
- Right.
- Damage report.

00:23:55.130 --> 00:23:56.757
We took six hits
on the port shields.

00:23:56.798 --> 00:23:58.129
There's been some minor damage

00:23:58.166 --> 00:24:00.498
to the outer hull,
but all systems are operational.

00:24:00.535 --> 00:24:02.093
Tough little ship.

00:24:02.137 --> 00:24:03.866
Set a course for the shipyard
at Omekla III.

00:24:03.905 --> 00:24:05.099
We'll let that be the place
that...

00:24:06.141 --> 00:24:07.199
Report.

00:24:07.242 --> 00:24:09.938
We've lost main power,
and the cloak is off-line.

00:24:10.011 --> 00:24:12.479
Looks like two plasma
conduits blew out.

00:24:12.514 --> 00:24:13.503
Where?

00:24:13.548 --> 00:24:16.745
Deck 3, section 15.

00:24:16.785 --> 00:24:17.877
Crew quarters.

00:24:20.822 --> 00:24:23.313
Looks like
Major Kira's been busy.

00:24:29.297 --> 00:24:31.390
You crossed the replicator
power converter

00:24:31.433 --> 00:24:32.627
with the plasma manifold,
I take it.

00:24:32.667 --> 00:24:33.725
That's right.

00:24:33.769 --> 00:24:34.861
Nice work.

00:24:34.903 --> 00:24:37.133
You know I'll have that thing
bypassed in 30 minutes.

00:24:37.172 --> 00:24:39.299
At least that'll be 30 minutes
that we're visible.

00:24:39.341 --> 00:24:41.605
Fortunately, I was able
to take us into a nebula.

00:24:41.643 --> 00:24:42.905
No one's going to see us.

00:24:44.146 --> 00:24:45.613
Thanks.

00:24:46.448 --> 00:24:48.279
You're lucky
you only got singed.

00:24:48.316 --> 00:24:50.250
You know, the whole plasma relay
could have exploded.

00:24:50.285 --> 00:24:51.684
Yeah, that was the idea.

00:24:51.720 --> 00:24:54.780
You've been fighting Cardassians
most of your life.

00:24:54.823 --> 00:24:57.121
I know that you sympathize
with what we're doing here.

00:24:57.159 --> 00:24:59.787
I fought the Cardassians
because they invaded my home.

00:24:59.828 --> 00:25:01.796
You don't live
in the Demilitarized Zone.

00:25:01.830 --> 00:25:03.195
You don't have family there.

00:25:03.231 --> 00:25:04.528
Why are you in this fight?

00:25:04.566 --> 00:25:07.399
Because people are dying
in the Demilitarized Zone

00:25:07.436 --> 00:25:09.563
and Starfleet isn't doing
anything about it.

00:25:09.604 --> 00:25:11.572
Taking the Defiant
only raises the stakes.

00:25:11.606 --> 00:25:14.074
The Cardassians are going
to send a fleet after you.

00:25:14.109 --> 00:25:16.543
They are going to kill
more people hunting you down

00:25:16.578 --> 00:25:18.705
than they ever did
during those border raids.

00:25:18.747 --> 00:25:20.681
You're assuming
the Defiant is going to stay

00:25:20.715 --> 00:25:21.875
in the Demilitarized Zone.

00:25:21.917 --> 00:25:23.578
Let's go to the Bridge.

00:25:23.618 --> 00:25:25.518
I think we'd all feel better
having you someplace

00:25:25.554 --> 00:25:26.612
we can keep an eye on you.

00:25:27.956 --> 00:25:30.891
15 outposts have checked in.

00:25:30.926 --> 00:25:33.588
No sign of the Defiant.

00:25:34.596 --> 00:25:35.961
26 warships have scanned

00:25:36.031 --> 00:25:39.728
14 cubic light-years of space
with antiproton beams...

00:25:39.768 --> 00:25:42.202
no Defiant!

00:25:42.237 --> 00:25:43.636
What are the possibilities?

00:25:43.672 --> 00:25:44.969
They're still under cloak

00:25:45.040 --> 00:25:47.167
and heading deeper
into Cardassian space.

00:25:47.209 --> 00:25:48.403
They're laying low

00:25:48.443 --> 00:25:52.072
and waiting
for some unknown reason.

00:25:52.113 --> 00:25:53.080
Dukat.

00:25:53.114 --> 00:25:54.081
Hmm?

00:25:54.115 --> 00:25:55.412
Are you listening to me?

00:25:55.450 --> 00:25:57.441
Oh, I'm sorry, Commander.

00:25:57.486 --> 00:26:00.614
I was thinking
about my son's birthday.

00:26:02.924 --> 00:26:04.391
Really?

00:26:04.426 --> 00:26:07.995
Yes, today is his 11th birthday.

00:26:08.128 --> 00:26:08.924
Oh.

00:26:08.996 --> 00:26:10.691
I'd promised to take him

00:26:10.731 --> 00:26:14.599
to the amusement center
in Lakarian City.

00:26:14.634 --> 00:26:17.467
He always wanted to go...

00:26:18.472 --> 00:26:20.702
but I never had the time.

00:26:22.009 --> 00:26:28.141
I told him, "This year
will be different, Mekor.

00:26:28.181 --> 00:26:32.311
This year,
I will make the time."

00:26:37.724 --> 00:26:40.818
I had the same experience
with Jake.

00:26:40.861 --> 00:26:44.957
At that age, they never
understand, do they?

00:26:44.998 --> 00:26:48.195
You just hope that,
one day later

00:26:48.235 --> 00:26:49.463
they'll look back and say

00:26:50.604 --> 00:26:52.970
"Now I understand.

00:26:53.040 --> 00:26:55.736
Now I know why he did that."

00:26:57.778 --> 00:27:02.681
When my son looks back
on this day

00:27:02.716 --> 00:27:05.082
the only thing he'll remember

00:27:05.118 --> 00:27:09.350
is that a Federation officer,
on a Federation ship

00:27:09.389 --> 00:27:12.358
invaded his home

00:27:12.392 --> 00:27:17.887
and kept his father away
from him on his 11th birthday

00:27:17.931 --> 00:27:21.162
and he won't look back
with understanding.

00:27:22.436 --> 00:27:25.428
He'll look back with hatred...

00:27:27.407 --> 00:27:29.568
and that's sad.

00:27:43.323 --> 00:27:45.587
The cloak is operating
within normal parameters

00:27:45.625 --> 00:27:47.183
but the plasma conduit damage

00:27:47.227 --> 00:27:50.196
has caused a slight neutrino
leak in the port nacelle.

00:27:50.230 --> 00:27:52.630
The Cardassians might
be able to detect it

00:27:52.666 --> 00:27:53.928
even through the cloak.

00:27:53.967 --> 00:27:55.298
A chance we have to take.

00:27:55.335 --> 00:27:57.235
Lay in the course
for Omekla III.

00:27:57.270 --> 00:27:58.464
Engage at warp eight.

00:27:58.505 --> 00:28:00.336
Warp eight.
Aye, sir.

00:28:00.373 --> 00:28:01.362
Omekla III?

00:28:01.408 --> 00:28:04.138
You're headed for the shipyard?

00:28:05.278 --> 00:28:06.802
There have to be
half a dozen better targets

00:28:06.847 --> 00:28:08.371
in this sector alone.

00:28:08.415 --> 00:28:10.906
I hope the Cardassians
have the same reaction.

00:28:10.951 --> 00:28:12.885
"What is he doing?

00:28:12.919 --> 00:28:14.147
And why?"

00:28:14.187 --> 00:28:16.052
All right, now you're trying

00:28:16.089 --> 00:28:18.887
to keep them off balance,
keep them guessing.

00:28:20.393 --> 00:28:21.382
Why?

00:28:22.729 --> 00:28:25.220
The Maquis
have been hearing rumors

00:28:25.265 --> 00:28:28.530
about shifting loyalties
in the Cardassian government.

00:28:28.568 --> 00:28:30.729
Certain hard-line elements
were unsatisfied

00:28:30.770 --> 00:28:32.135
with the Federation treaty

00:28:32.172 --> 00:28:34.470
and are doing whatever
they can to scrap it.

00:28:36.409 --> 00:28:38.877
We got our hands
on an intelligence report

00:28:38.912 --> 00:28:43.178
outlining suspected military
buildup in the Orias system...

00:28:43.216 --> 00:28:46.276
a secret buildup that even the
Central Command isn't aware of.

00:28:46.319 --> 00:28:49.550
You're telling me
you did all of this

00:28:49.589 --> 00:28:53.218
to attack some secret base
that may or may not exist?

00:28:53.260 --> 00:28:55.728
I'm convinced that it does.

00:28:55.762 --> 00:28:57.957
They are building
an invasion fleet.

00:28:57.998 --> 00:28:59.590
If we let them finish it

00:28:59.633 --> 00:29:03.091
these renegade Cardassians
are going to use it.

00:29:07.641 --> 00:29:09.871
You're really not cut out
for this, are you?

00:29:09.910 --> 00:29:12.037
Being a terrorist, I mean.

00:29:14.247 --> 00:29:16.044
You're not very good at it.

00:29:16.082 --> 00:29:17.174
Really?

00:29:17.217 --> 00:29:19.310
You're acting more like
a Starfleet officer

00:29:19.352 --> 00:29:22.480
who's more interested
in intelligence reports

00:29:22.522 --> 00:29:27.152
and Cardassian politics, than
in actually hurting Cardassians.

00:29:28.662 --> 00:29:30.926
You have one
of the most powerful ships

00:29:31.031 --> 00:29:33.226
in this Quadrant
under your command.

00:29:33.266 --> 00:29:36.394
Why aren't you out attacking
every Cardassian outpost

00:29:36.436 --> 00:29:37.460
along the border?

00:29:37.504 --> 00:29:39.631
Because these stakes
are far greater

00:29:39.673 --> 00:29:41.163
than border outposts.

00:29:41.208 --> 00:29:42.766
Not for the Maquis, they're not

00:29:42.809 --> 00:29:44.936
because the Maquis
are terrorists

00:29:44.978 --> 00:29:46.809
and the only thing
terrorists care about

00:29:46.846 --> 00:29:48.609
is attacking the enemy.

00:29:48.648 --> 00:29:49.945
I know...
I was a terrorist

00:29:49.983 --> 00:29:52.952
and if I had had this ship then

00:29:53.019 --> 00:29:54.850
I would have destroyed
Deep Space 9.

00:29:54.888 --> 00:29:56.879
I would have hit
the Cardassians so hard

00:29:56.923 --> 00:29:58.151
they would have
screamed for peace.

00:29:58.191 --> 00:30:00.921
But I certainly wouldn't
have gone flying off

00:30:00.961 --> 00:30:04.863
into the middle of Cardassia
on some wild-goose chase.

00:30:04.898 --> 00:30:07.731
I guess we're different
kinds of terrorists.

00:30:07.767 --> 00:30:09.792
No...

00:30:09.836 --> 00:30:11.827
you're trying to be a hero.

00:30:12.839 --> 00:30:15.501
Terrorists don't get
to be heroes.

00:30:17.344 --> 00:30:19.835
We'll see.

00:30:19.913 --> 00:30:22.473
This is how
your ships were deployed

00:30:22.515 --> 00:30:24.540
before the first Defiant attack.

00:30:24.584 --> 00:30:26.575
And this is where they are now.

00:30:28.822 --> 00:30:30.255
Don't you see what happened?

00:30:30.290 --> 00:30:31.951
Each Defiant attack
was designed

00:30:31.992 --> 00:30:34.256
to draw your ships
away from that sector

00:30:34.294 --> 00:30:36.626
leaving it virtually
defenseless.

00:30:36.663 --> 00:30:39.496
But there's nothing
of any value in that sector.

00:30:39.532 --> 00:30:41.193
There must be something.

00:30:41.234 --> 00:30:43.725
Are there any M-Class
planets there?

00:30:43.770 --> 00:30:45.169
Well, there's one...

00:30:45.205 --> 00:30:47.901
Orias III, but it's uninhabited.

00:30:47.941 --> 00:30:48.999
It's desolate.

00:30:49.075 --> 00:30:51.908
But everything seems to point
to the Orias system.

00:30:51.945 --> 00:30:55.176
It might be worth your sending
one of your warships there

00:30:55.215 --> 00:30:57.410
just in case
the Defiant does show up.

00:30:59.452 --> 00:31:00.851
All right.

00:31:00.887 --> 00:31:02.411
Contact Gul Ranor.

00:31:02.455 --> 00:31:05.515
Tell him to dispatch
one warship...

00:31:05.558 --> 00:31:06.582
No.

00:31:07.794 --> 00:31:10.388
You'll send no ships
to the Orias system.

00:31:10.430 --> 00:31:12.125
You're here as an observer.

00:31:12.165 --> 00:31:13.598
You have no authority.

00:31:13.633 --> 00:31:14.657
That sector is

00:31:14.701 --> 00:31:17.067
under direct control
of the Obsidian Order

00:31:17.103 --> 00:31:18.593
and you will not enter it.

00:31:18.638 --> 00:31:19.764
Why?!

00:31:19.806 --> 00:31:21.671
That matter's classified.

00:31:21.708 --> 00:31:22.970
Well.

00:31:23.043 --> 00:31:27.810
You can file a complaint
with the Central Command later.

00:31:27.847 --> 00:31:30.475
Open a channel
to Gul Ranor now.

00:31:30.517 --> 00:31:32.781
Any warship sent
into the Orias system

00:31:32.819 --> 00:31:34.548
will be destroyed.

00:31:34.587 --> 00:31:37.249
Are you saying
that you will fire

00:31:37.290 --> 00:31:39.485
on another Cardassian ship?

00:31:39.526 --> 00:31:42.620
What I am saying is
that the Obsidian Order

00:31:42.662 --> 00:31:45.392
will take whatever steps
are necessary

00:31:45.432 --> 00:31:47.491
to protect the Orias system.

00:31:47.534 --> 00:31:49.331
And so will I.

00:32:10.990 --> 00:32:14.289
I've spoken to a few friends
in the Central Command.

00:32:14.327 --> 00:32:16.795
The Obsidian Order isn't giving
them any answers, either.

00:32:16.830 --> 00:32:19.162
The Order has to answer
to someone.

00:32:19.199 --> 00:32:20.564
In theory, they answer

00:32:20.600 --> 00:32:23.626
to the political authority
of the Detapa Council

00:32:23.670 --> 00:32:25.331
just as the military does.

00:32:25.372 --> 00:32:28.136
In practice, we both
run our own affairs.

00:32:28.174 --> 00:32:29.869
Not a very efficient system.

00:32:29.909 --> 00:32:32.639
It's worked
for over five centuries.

00:32:32.679 --> 00:32:36.843
There's an incoming message
from the Warship Kraxon.

00:32:36.883 --> 00:32:39.317
They say they've found
an unusual neutrino signature

00:32:39.352 --> 00:32:40.376
in their sector.

00:32:40.420 --> 00:32:41.887
It looks like radiation

00:32:41.921 --> 00:32:43.855
from a damaged
warp plasma relay.

00:32:43.890 --> 00:32:45.585
Is this signature moving?

00:32:45.625 --> 00:32:48.116
No, but they're scanning
their area

00:32:48.161 --> 00:32:50.186
with their antiproton beams.

00:32:50.230 --> 00:32:51.458
Where is the Kraxon?

00:32:57.170 --> 00:32:59.536
If it is the Defiant,
they're in position

00:32:59.572 --> 00:33:01.597
to make a run
for the Orias system.

00:33:01.641 --> 00:33:04.633
We still don't know
that Orias is the target.

00:33:04.677 --> 00:33:06.372
Until we do, I can't risk

00:33:06.413 --> 00:33:09.610
pulling ships away from
other potential targets

00:33:09.649 --> 00:33:12.174
to chase down
a neutrino signature.

00:33:14.819 --> 00:33:16.480
They're coming around
for another pass.

00:33:16.521 --> 00:33:18.318
Are there any other ships
nearby?

00:33:18.356 --> 00:33:21.052
There are nine
Galor-class cruisers

00:33:21.092 --> 00:33:22.389
about six light-years away.

00:33:22.427 --> 00:33:24.520
Any ships between us
and the Orias system?

00:33:24.562 --> 00:33:25.529
No.

00:33:25.563 --> 00:33:26.689
If you make a run for it

00:33:26.731 --> 00:33:27.857
that ship out there's
going to see

00:33:27.899 --> 00:33:29.799
our neutrino signature
go through a phase change.

00:33:29.834 --> 00:33:31.233
They're going to call
their nine friends

00:33:31.269 --> 00:33:32.827
and you are going to have
a small fleet

00:33:32.870 --> 00:33:34.235
chasing you
all the way to Orias.

00:33:34.272 --> 00:33:37.673
They can chase me
all they want...

00:33:37.709 --> 00:33:39.677
as long as they don't catch me.

00:33:39.711 --> 00:33:40.973
The Kraxon reports

00:33:41.012 --> 00:33:43.776
that the neutrino signature
has just phase-shifted

00:33:43.815 --> 00:33:45.976
and is moving now at warp speed

00:33:46.050 --> 00:33:48.314
directly
toward the Orias system.

00:33:48.352 --> 00:33:51.480
Order the Kraxon
to pursue at maximum warp.

00:33:51.522 --> 00:33:54.491
Order all other ships
in the sector to follow.

00:33:54.525 --> 00:33:56.356
The Kraxon is pursuing

00:33:56.394 --> 00:33:58.123
but they won't catch us
before we reach Orias.

00:33:58.162 --> 00:33:59.322
Full scan.

00:33:59.363 --> 00:34:01.797
I want to see everything
that's in that system.

00:34:03.334 --> 00:34:06.167
When you make out your report
for the Obsidian Order

00:34:06.204 --> 00:34:09.332
be sure to mention the fact
that I could have prevented

00:34:09.373 --> 00:34:11.933
the Defiant from reaching Orias,
if you hadn't interfered.

00:34:11.976 --> 00:34:14.376
They will never reach Orias.

00:34:14.412 --> 00:34:16.346
You can count on that.

00:34:16.380 --> 00:34:18.405
Three more ships
have just appeared

00:34:18.449 --> 00:34:19.746
in the Orias system.

00:34:19.784 --> 00:34:21.411
What kind of ships?

00:34:21.452 --> 00:34:25.252
Cardassian warships...
Keldon-class.

00:34:25.289 --> 00:34:27.951
Whose ships are those, Korinas?

00:34:27.992 --> 00:34:29.960
Why are you asking me?

00:34:29.994 --> 00:34:32.360
Because if they
were military ships

00:34:32.396 --> 00:34:33.954
I would know about them.

00:34:34.065 --> 00:34:36.465
So that leaves
the Obsidian Order.

00:34:36.501 --> 00:34:39.368
I thought the Obsidian Order
didn't have any ships.

00:34:39.403 --> 00:34:40.768
They're not supposed to.

00:34:40.805 --> 00:34:42.932
In fact, they are
explicitly forbidden

00:34:42.974 --> 00:34:46.603
from having military equipment
of any kind.

00:34:53.050 --> 00:34:55.575
It looks like we're going to
have to fight our way to Orias.

00:34:55.620 --> 00:34:56.780
Listen to me.

00:34:56.821 --> 00:34:58.584
Those three ships up ahead

00:34:58.623 --> 00:35:01.922
are going to lock onto our
neutrino leak and open fire.

00:35:01.993 --> 00:35:03.858
That means you're going
to have to fight back.

00:35:03.895 --> 00:35:06.159
With this ship, it'll be a short
fight, I promise you that.

00:35:06.197 --> 00:35:07.721
Let's say you disable

00:35:07.765 --> 00:35:10.233
or even destroy, those
three ships up ahead of us.

00:35:10.268 --> 00:35:12.532
Fighting them at all
is going to slow us down.

00:35:12.570 --> 00:35:14.231
And then those ten ships
behind us

00:35:14.272 --> 00:35:15.466
are going to catch up.

00:35:15.506 --> 00:35:17.838
And not even the Defiant
can win against those odds.

00:35:17.875 --> 00:35:19.342
We have come too far
to quit now.

00:35:19.377 --> 00:35:22.346
You are an experienced
Starfleet officer, Tom.

00:35:22.380 --> 00:35:23.813
Analyze the situation.

00:35:23.848 --> 00:35:25.543
Going to Orias is suicide.

00:35:25.583 --> 00:35:29.417
Now, the smart move is to make
a run for it while we still can.

00:35:29.453 --> 00:35:32.820
Maybe that's what an experienced
Starfleet officer would do

00:35:32.857 --> 00:35:34.324
maybe that's what
Will Riker would do

00:35:34.358 --> 00:35:36.292
but it's not
what I'm going to do.

00:35:36.327 --> 00:35:37.760
I'm going to continue
the mission.

00:35:37.795 --> 00:35:39.786
It's not the mission
you're thinking about, is it?

00:35:39.831 --> 00:35:41.696
Or even the colonists
in the Zone.

00:35:41.732 --> 00:35:43.097
This is about you, isn't it?

00:35:43.134 --> 00:35:44.965
You and that other Will Riker
out there.

00:35:45.036 --> 00:35:47.231
The man with your face,
your name, your career.

00:35:47.271 --> 00:35:49.865
You are looking for a way
to set yourself apart.

00:35:49.907 --> 00:35:51.306
Some way to be different.

00:35:51.342 --> 00:35:53.742
You shouldn't go fishing today.

00:35:53.778 --> 00:35:55.769
You won't catch anything.

00:35:57.281 --> 00:35:58.646
Take us in.

00:36:08.826 --> 00:36:12.887
You want to know what's going on
in the Orias system

00:36:12.930 --> 00:36:15.194
I know how you can find out.

00:36:15.233 --> 00:36:17.531
Give Riker a chance
to surrender.

00:36:17.568 --> 00:36:20.765
The Defiant's scanned
the Orias system by now.

00:36:20.805 --> 00:36:24.798
Its sensor logs can tell you
everything you want to know.

00:36:24.842 --> 00:36:27.333
I'd be happy to accept
his surrender

00:36:27.378 --> 00:36:29.938
but I doubt he'll be willing
to hand over his logs.

00:36:30.014 --> 00:36:32.539
He will, if you agree
to release Major Kira

00:36:32.583 --> 00:36:35.711
turn the ship and the Maquis
over to the Federation.

00:36:35.753 --> 00:36:36.845
Impossible!

00:36:36.888 --> 00:36:39.652
I cannot allow a group
of terrorists

00:36:39.690 --> 00:36:43.319
to just walk away
after invading our territory...

00:36:43.361 --> 00:36:46.387
Then you must decide
which is important to you...

00:36:46.430 --> 00:36:48.330
your sense of Cardassian justice

00:36:48.366 --> 00:36:52.029
or the information contained
in the Defiant's sensor logs.

00:36:53.504 --> 00:36:56.735
I do want that information,
Commander

00:36:56.774 --> 00:37:00.335
and I would be willing
to return your wayward ship

00:37:00.378 --> 00:37:02.903
but someone has to pay
for what's happened here

00:37:02.980 --> 00:37:05.278
and I don't want
that someone to be me.

00:37:05.316 --> 00:37:07.546
If you return the Maquis
to the Federation

00:37:07.585 --> 00:37:09.917
I can promise you
that they will stand trial

00:37:10.021 --> 00:37:11.215
for what they've done.

00:37:11.255 --> 00:37:13.086
A Federation trial.

00:37:13.124 --> 00:37:14.853
It's the best I can do.

00:37:15.993 --> 00:37:17.517
All right.

00:37:17.561 --> 00:37:21.429
I would be willing to hand over

00:37:21.465 --> 00:37:25.697
Major Kira, the Maquis
and the ship

00:37:25.736 --> 00:37:27.397
but not Riker.

00:37:27.438 --> 00:37:29.736
He led the mission.

00:37:29.774 --> 00:37:32.504
If I can bring him to justice

00:37:32.543 --> 00:37:35.910
and obtain the information
on Orias

00:37:35.947 --> 00:37:39.144
that might be enough
for Central Command.

00:37:51.896 --> 00:37:55.730
I might be able to get him
to do it, on one condition.

00:37:55.766 --> 00:37:58.428
We both know
that Cardassian sentences

00:37:58.469 --> 00:38:01.632
are determined
well in advance of the trial.

00:38:01.672 --> 00:38:05.665
I'd like you to arrange
a sentence other than death.

00:38:10.381 --> 00:38:14.408
I'll have to clear that
with the Ministry of Justice.

00:38:15.619 --> 00:38:17.484
You'd better make it quick.

00:38:28.699 --> 00:38:30.758
We're approaching
the first cruiser.

00:38:30.801 --> 00:38:33.133
They'll be in phaser range
in 15 seconds.

00:38:34.472 --> 00:38:35.632
Go to impulse.

00:38:35.673 --> 00:38:36.935
De-cloak the ship.

00:38:36.974 --> 00:38:39.943
Raise shields
and stand by phasers.

00:38:40.011 --> 00:38:43.947
Go to heading 118 mark 310.

00:38:44.048 --> 00:38:46.608
Lock on phasers.

00:38:46.650 --> 00:38:48.208
Fire.

00:38:52.223 --> 00:38:54.953
Direct hit on the cruiser's
port nacelle.

00:38:55.059 --> 00:38:57.619
Their shields
are down by 30 percent.

00:38:57.661 --> 00:38:59.891
We've been hit
on our starboard shield.

00:39:07.038 --> 00:39:08.733
Shields holding.

00:39:08.773 --> 00:39:10.741
Quantum torpedoes...
full spread.

00:39:10.775 --> 00:39:12.208
Torpedoes locked on target.

00:39:12.243 --> 00:39:13.471
Fire!

00:39:18.315 --> 00:39:19.907
Their defense systems
are off-line

00:39:19.984 --> 00:39:22.418
and they've lost main power.

00:39:22.453 --> 00:39:23.420
Tom, three more cruisers

00:39:23.454 --> 00:39:24.887
have just appeared
in the Orias system.

00:39:24.922 --> 00:39:26.822
That makes five ships
ahead of us and ten behind.

00:39:28.626 --> 00:39:31.288
Resume our original course
to the Orias system.

00:39:31.328 --> 00:39:33.421
Stand by emergency
power to the shields.

00:39:33.464 --> 00:39:35.932
Incoming message
from Cardassia Prime.

00:39:36.000 --> 00:39:39.128
It's Gul Dukat
and Commander Sisko.

00:39:41.572 --> 00:39:43.062
On screen.

00:39:43.107 --> 00:39:46.133
This is Gul Dukat
of the Second Order.

00:39:46.177 --> 00:39:49.874
I am authorized to tell you
that if you surrender your ship

00:39:49.914 --> 00:39:52.144
none of you will be harmed.

00:39:52.183 --> 00:39:53.411
Is that right?

00:39:55.486 --> 00:39:56.953
Listen to him, Lieutenant.

00:39:57.054 --> 00:39:59.545
If you surrender,
the Defiant and its crew

00:39:59.590 --> 00:40:02.184
will be handed over
to a Federation starship

00:40:02.226 --> 00:40:03.716
at the Cardassian border.

00:40:03.761 --> 00:40:05.353
Why the sudden generosity?

00:40:05.396 --> 00:40:08.797
He wants the Defiant's sensor
logs on the Orias system.

00:40:08.833 --> 00:40:12.269
They're worth a lot more
to him than Maquis prisoners.

00:40:12.303 --> 00:40:13.803
I don't buy it.

00:40:13.936 --> 00:40:16.928
The Cardassians aren't going
to just let us walk away.

00:40:16.972 --> 00:40:18.064
You're right.

00:40:18.107 --> 00:40:21.008
Someone has to pay the price.

00:40:22.344 --> 00:40:23.311
Me.

00:40:23.345 --> 00:40:25.336
The deal is

00:40:25.381 --> 00:40:28.077
you'll be tried and convicted
in a Cardassian court

00:40:28.117 --> 00:40:30.711
and then sentenced
to spend the rest of your life

00:40:30.753 --> 00:40:33.688
in the Lazon II labor camp.

00:40:33.722 --> 00:40:36.088
No death sentence, huh?

00:40:36.125 --> 00:40:38.286
That must have taken some doing.

00:40:39.795 --> 00:40:40.819
Some.

00:40:40.863 --> 00:40:43.559
Give me a moment.

00:40:50.039 --> 00:40:51.404
Tom.

00:40:54.743 --> 00:40:57.371
There's no reason
for you to continue.

00:40:57.413 --> 00:40:58.812
They're offering you a way out.

00:40:58.848 --> 00:41:01.442
The only reason not to take it
is because you want to die.

00:41:01.483 --> 00:41:03.075
I have a mission to complete.

00:41:03.118 --> 00:41:04.176
That mission is over.

00:41:04.220 --> 00:41:06.518
You're never going
to make it to Orias.

00:41:06.555 --> 00:41:07.681
You know that, Tom.

00:41:07.723 --> 00:41:10.191
There are five ships
out there ahead of you

00:41:10.226 --> 00:41:13.195
but there may be 50 waiting
there, for all we know.

00:41:13.229 --> 00:41:16.392
Be a Starfleet
officer one last time.

00:41:16.432 --> 00:41:18.093
Think of your crew.

00:41:18.133 --> 00:41:20.897
I know you want Tom Riker
to go out in a blaze of glory

00:41:20.936 --> 00:41:23.131
that they talk about
for the next ten years.

00:41:23.172 --> 00:41:26.335
Don't drag them along with you.

00:41:34.550 --> 00:41:35.608
On screen.

00:41:39.488 --> 00:41:41.080
I agree to your terms.

00:41:41.123 --> 00:41:44.889
You need to reverse course
and surrender the Defiant

00:41:44.927 --> 00:41:46.918
to one of the ships
that's been following you.

00:41:46.962 --> 00:41:47.951
Why?

00:41:47.997 --> 00:41:49.760
It will take too long to explain

00:41:49.798 --> 00:41:52.494
but the ships coming out
of the Orias system

00:41:52.534 --> 00:41:54.627
are not
under Gul Dukat's control.

00:41:54.670 --> 00:41:55.637
I see.

00:41:55.671 --> 00:41:57.002
I've ordered the Kraxon

00:41:57.072 --> 00:42:00.166
to put her shields around you
as soon as you arrive.

00:42:00.209 --> 00:42:02.234
You'll be safe
once you get there.

00:42:02.278 --> 00:42:03.711
Understood.

00:42:09.184 --> 00:42:10.208
Turn us about.

00:42:10.252 --> 00:42:12.243
Lay in a course for the Kraxon.

00:42:13.789 --> 00:42:14.915
Do it.

00:42:22.498 --> 00:42:25.126
Those are faster
than any Keldon-class ships

00:42:25.167 --> 00:42:27.135
I've ever seen.

00:42:27.169 --> 00:42:29.729
What is going on in that system?

00:42:30.940 --> 00:42:33.170
We're 100 million kilometers
from the Kraxon.

00:42:33.208 --> 00:42:34.402
Incoming message.

00:42:34.443 --> 00:42:35.671
Let's hear it.

00:42:35.711 --> 00:42:37.611
This is Gul Ranor of the Kraxon.

00:42:37.646 --> 00:42:39.546
Cut your engines in five seconds

00:42:39.581 --> 00:42:41.981
and we will extend
our shields around you.

00:42:42.084 --> 00:42:43.949
Acknowledged.

00:42:43.986 --> 00:42:45.044
Kalita.

00:42:47.957 --> 00:42:49.117
All stop.

00:43:13.382 --> 00:43:16.681
They won't fire
on another Cardassian ship.

00:43:17.886 --> 00:43:19.183
They can't.

00:43:23.792 --> 00:43:25.487
They're moving off.

00:43:25.527 --> 00:43:28.087
They've set course
back to the Orias system.

00:43:28.130 --> 00:43:31.224
Transmit the Orias III
sensor logs to the Kraxon

00:43:31.266 --> 00:43:34.565
and tell them to prepare
to beam me aboard.

00:43:34.603 --> 00:43:37.367
I'm turning command over
to Major Kira.

00:43:37.406 --> 00:43:40.432
She'll get you back
to the Federation.

00:43:40.476 --> 00:43:42.501
I'm holding you
personally responsible

00:43:42.544 --> 00:43:44.808
to see that these people get
a fair trial.

00:43:44.847 --> 00:43:47.179
I give you my word.

00:43:49.752 --> 00:43:51.845
We'll get you out of there, Tom.

00:43:51.887 --> 00:43:53.548
I promise you that.

00:44:11.273 --> 00:44:12.365
Riker to Kraxon.

00:44:12.408 --> 00:44:13.534
Go ahead.

00:44:13.575 --> 00:44:15.236
